1:{ev:["Pip visits his parents' graves in the marsh churchyard on Christmas Eve.","A terrifying convict seizes Pip among the gravestones and demands a file and food.","Pip promises to help him and runs home in fear.","Before dawn, Pip steals a pork pie, brandy and Joe's file from the pantry.","On the misty marsh, Pip mistakes a second convict for his own.","Pip finds his convict, who eats like a starving animal and asks furiously about the other man."],keys:["graves","seizes","promises","steals","mistakes","starving"]},
2:{ev:["Pip sits through an agonising Christmas dinner with Wopsle, Hubble and Pumblechook.","Soldiers interrupt the meal, asking Joe to mend broken handcuffs.","Joe, Pip and Wopsle join the soldiers hunting two escaped convicts across the marsh.","The two convicts are found fighting fiercely in a ditch.","Pip's convict confesses to stealing the food himself, protecting Pip.","Joe says gently that the convict was welcome to it, and the men are rowed back to the prison ship."],keys:["dinner","handcuffs","hunting","ditch","confesses","rowed"]},
3:{ev:["Pumblechook takes Pip to play at Miss Havisham's Satis House.","Pip meets Miss Havisham, sitting in her old, yellowed wedding dress among stopped clocks.","Estella leads Pip away to play cards, mocking his coarse hands and boots.","Pip feels ashamed of himself for the first time in his life.","Back home, Pip invents wild lies about his visit to Satis House.","Pip confesses the truth to Joe, who tells him that lying is no way to become uncommon."],keys:["play","clocks","mocking","ashamed","invents","confesses"]},
4:{ev:["Biddy teaches Pip his letters at the evening school.","A stranger at the Jolly Bargemen stirs his drink with Joe's file and gives Pip two pounds.","Pip spends months pushing Miss Havisham's chair around Satis House.","A pale young gentleman challenges Pip to a fight in the garden and loses.","Estella allows Pip to kiss her cheek as a reward.","Miss Havisham pays twenty-five guineas for Pip to be apprenticed to Joe."],keys:["teaches","stirs","pushing","challenges","allows","pays"]},
5:{ev:["Pip grows unhappy as Joe's apprentice, ashamed of the forge and dreaming of Estella.","Orlick, the surly journeyman, quarrels violently with Mrs Joe.","Mrs Joe is struck down and badly injured, and never speaks properly again.","Biddy comes to keep house and nurse Mrs Joe.","Mr Jaggers, a lawyer, tells Pip he has great expectations from a secret benefactor.","Pip assumes Miss Havisham is his benefactor and leaves for London, patronising Joe and Biddy."],keys:["dreaming","quarrels","struck","keep","expectations","patronising"]},
6:{ev:["Pip visits Mr Jaggers's gloomy office and meets his clerk Wemmick.","Pip discovers his room-mate at Barnard's Inn is Herbert Pocket, who renames him Handel.","Herbert tells Pip the story of Miss Havisham's jilting by a swindler.","Pip studies at Hammersmith with sulky Drummle and cheerful Startop.","Wemmick shows Pip his cheerful Castle at Walworth and the Aged Parent.","At dinner, Mr Jaggers silently shows the scars on his housekeeper Molly's wrist."],keys:["meets","renames","jilting","studies","shows","scars"]},
7:{ev:["Joe visits Pip in London, feeling out of place among his new friends.","Joe tells Pip, with quiet dignity, that they belong to different lines of life.","Pip discovers Orlick now works as Miss Havisham's gatekeeper.","Miss Havisham urges Pip to love the now beautiful Estella.","Herbert confesses he is secretly engaged to Clara.","Estella warns Pip on the way to Richmond that she has no heart."],keys:["visits","dignity","gatekeeper","urges","engaged","warns"]},
8:{ev:["Pip and Herbert fall into serious debt with the Finches of the Grove.","Pip returns home for his sister's funeral and promises Biddy he will visit.","Pip secretly arranges a partnership for Herbert through Wemmick.","Estella is courted by Bentley Drummle at Richmond, tormenting Pip.","Miss Havisham and Estella quarrel bitterly about coldness.","A weathered stranger climbs the stairs on a stormy night and reveals he is Pip's true benefactor."],keys:["debt","funeral","arranges","courted","quarrel","reveals"]},
9:{ev:["Pip and Herbert hide Magwitch in Essex Street under the alias Mr Provis.","Magwitch tells his story of childhood poverty and crime.","Magwitch describes his partnership with the dishonest gentleman Compeyson.","Compeyson receives a lighter sentence than Magwitch at their trial.","Pip realises Compeyson jilted Miss Havisham and fought Magwitch on the marsh.","Pip resolves to help plan Magwitch's escape from England."],keys:["hide","poverty","partnership","sentence","realises","escape"]},
10:{ev:["Pip accuses Miss Havisham of cruelty and she agrees to finish paying for Herbert.","Estella announces she will marry Bentley Drummle, rejecting Pip completely.","Wemmick warns Pip not to go home because Compeyson is watching.","Magwitch is moved secretly to a house by the river at Mill Pond Bank.","Mr Wopsle recognises Compeyson sitting behind Pip at the theatre.","Pip notices a strange resemblance between Molly and Estella."],keys:["accuses","announces","warns","moved","recognises","resemblance"]},
